' Business/Product: ../../01-business/BRD.md (v0.3); ../../02-product/PRD.md (v0.2)
' Master Actors/Scope: ../use-cases/use-case-diagram.puml
' Process Authority: ../../../Initial files/CapsuleAI_Scrum_Development_Workflow.md, Sections 11, 39–42, 46
' Version: 0.1; Status: Baseline Draft
' SRS trace: FR-WEAR-001, FR-WEAR-002, FR-WEAR-003, FR-WEAR-004, FR-WEAR-009, FR-WEAR-010, FR-WEAR-011, DATA-WEAR-002, DATA-INT-004, ERR-WEAR-001
' Rule trace: BRULE-AUTH-001, BRULE-WEAR-001, BRULE-WEAR-002, BRULE-WEAR-003, BRULE-WEAR-006, BRULE-PERS-005
' Flow coverage: UC Sections 6–10; alternatives and failures retain their textual meaning.
' The textual Use Case Specification remains the normative behavioral source.

title AD-014 - Record Wear Event
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false

|User|
start
:Explicitly initiate Wear This Today for owned outfit;
|CapsuleAI|
if (Authorized access usable?) then (Yes)
    :Identify logical intention, outfit and available context;
else (No)
    :Pause protected use; require renewed access (UC-002);
    stop
endif
repeat
    if (This logical action already accepted?) then (Yes)
        :Return its single accepted event;
        :Do not create another report or evidence increment;
        stop
    endif
    if (Outfit currently eligible and valid?) then (Yes)
        :Attempt acceptance of this reporting intention;
    else (No)
        :Explain changed ownership/readiness/validity;
        :Create no new accepted event;
        |User|
        :Refresh/correct existing inputs before a new valid report;
        stop
    endif
    |CapsuleAI|
    if (Acceptance established?) then (Yes)
        :Create one distinct user-reported Wear Event;
        :Default time to accepted current time;
        :Preserve absolute timestamp, original local date/time
and event timezone/UTC offset;
        :Update effective history and utilization;
        :Update recency and normalized age-weighted evidence;
        note right
          Each new explicit intention remains a separate event,
          including another report for the same outfit/day.
          One outfit/original-day group supplies at most one
          Wear increment, anchored at its latest accepted event.
          Absolute elapsed time governs aging and recency.
        end note
        :Show accepted user-reported event;
        |User|
        :Review history or continue wardrobe use;
        stop
    else (Rejected / unconfirmed)
        |CapsuleAI|
        :Distinguish known failure from uncertain outcome;
        :Do not claim acceptance or definite absence
from an uncertain response;
        |User|
        :Review history or retry the same logical action;
    endif
repeat while (Retry this same intention?) is (Yes) not (No)
|CapsuleAI|
:End without a false acceptance or duplicate event;
stop

@enduml
